#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:4
msgid "Step 9: Using the Command Line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:8
msgid ""
"This step extends :ref:`Step 8 <CTest Dashboard Step 8>` by replacing the "
"dashboard script with :program:`ctest` command lines in a shell script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:11
msgid "Step9/submit.sh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:11
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"\n"
"cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\n"
"site=$(uname -n)\n"
"presets=\"$(pwd)/../Step8/CMakePresets.json\"\n"
"rm -rf build\n"
"\n"
"# Start a new dashboard and configure an empty build tree.\n"
"ctest -T Start -T Configure -T Submit \\\n"
"  --source-dir ../Project \\\n"
"  --build-dir build \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_BUILD_NAME=\"Step9: command line\" \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_SITE=\"$site\" \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_PRESET=coverage \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_PRESETS_FILE=\"$presets\" \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_SUBMIT_PARTS=Configure\n"
"\n"
"# Report the current Git commit.\n"
"ctest -T Update -T Submit \\\n"
"  --build-dir build \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_UPDATE_COMMAND=git \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_UPDATE_VERSION_ONLY=1 \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_SUBMIT_PARTS=Update\n"
"\n"
"# Build.\n"
"ctest -T Build -T Submit \\\n"
"  --build-dir build \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_PRESET=coverage \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_PRESETS_FILE=\"$presets\" \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_USE_LAUNCHERS=1 \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_SUBMIT_PARTS=Build\n"
"\n"
"# Test.\n"
"ctest -T Test -T Submit \\\n"
"  --build-dir build \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_PRESET=coverage \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_PRESETS_FILE=\"$presets\" \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_SUBMIT_PARTS=Test\n"
"\n"
"# Compute coverage, and tell CDash the build is done.\n"
"ctest -T Coverage -T Submit \\\n"
"  --build-dir build \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_SUBMIT_PARTS=\"Coverage;Done\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:15
msgid ""
"Each :program:`ctest` invocation runs the steps given by :option:`ctest -T`, "
"and sets variables with :option:`-D \\<var\\>=\\<value\\> <ctest-dashboard "
"-D>` instead of the :command:`set` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:20
msgid ""
"The first invocation configures an empty build tree, using the :ctest-"
"dashboard-option:`--source-dir` and :ctest-dashboard-option:`--build-dir` "
"options.  The later invocations run in that build tree and add their results "
"to the same submission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:25
msgid ""
"Each invocation ends with a ``Submit`` step.  "
"The :variable:`CTEST_SUBMIT_PARTS` variable limits it to the results of that "
"invocation, so that earlier results are not submitted again.  The last "
"invocation also submits the ``Done`` part, which tells CDash that the build "
"is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:31
msgid "A dashboard script and command lines each have advantages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:33
msgid ""
"A script can use the CMake language for logic, such as loops and conditions, "
"and keeps every step in one file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using the Command Line.rst:35
msgid ""
"Command lines can run the steps separately, such as in different jobs of a "
"CI pipeline, and need no ``.cmake`` file."
msgstr ""

